<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  ttyd Terminal-Bridge LaunchAgent — XACA-0161-002
  ================================================
  ONE JOB PER TERMINAL. Rendered by scripts/kb-ttyd-bridge.sh from the team
  board's `terminals` map; one plist per (team, terminal) pair, labelled
  com.aiteamforge.ttyd-bridge.<team>.<terminal>.

  WHY ONE JOB PER TERMINAL AND NOT ONE SUPERVISOR
  ----------------------------------------------
  A single supervising job that forks N ttyd children was considered and
  rejected on three grounds:

    1. It reinvents launchd. KeepAlive/ThrottleInterval already give per-process
       supervision, restart-on-crash and crash-loop damping. A supervisor would
       reimplement all of it, worse.
    2. Failure isolation. This mirrors the explicit rationale on the sibling
       per-team CR poller (install-kanban.sh): "isolating one LaunchAgent per
       team means a bad team config only wedges that team's poller; others keep
       running." A terminal whose tmux session is missing must not take down the
       three that are healthy.
    3. AbandonProcessGroup hazard (XACA-0763-002). launchd SIGKILLs every process
       left in a job's process group the instant the job itself exits. A
       supervisor that spawns ttyd children and returns would have them reaped
       out from under it; keeping the supervisor resident to avoid that is just
       launchd again, in shell.

  Per-terminal jobs also give per-terminal `launchctl list` visibility and
  per-terminal teardown, which is what makes the uninstall path verifiable.

  SECURITY POSTURE (see docs/xaca-0161-terminal-bridge-evaluation.md)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  * `-i lo0`  — loopback ONLY. Measured: `lsof` shows 127.0.0.1:<port> and
    nothing else; a probe from this host's LAN address returns exit=7. The
    UNIX-domain-socket form documented upstream returns 502 through
    `tailscale serve` on this machine and is deliberately NOT used here.
  * NO `-W`  — read-only by default. ttyd logs "will start in readonly mode".
    The writable variant is opt-in and renders an explicit <string>-W</string>
    in place of the {{WRITABLE_ARG}} line below; when read-only, the renderer
    DELETES that line rather than emitting an empty <string/>, which ttyd would
    otherwise receive as a stray empty argv entry.
  * `-H X-WEBAUTH-USER` — ttyd answers 407 to any request WITHOUT a non-empty
    X-WEBAUTH-USER header, on EVERY endpoint (index, /token and /ws alike;
    measured). The proxy is therefore the only usable caller, and it must inject
    that header on every proxied request, not just the WebSocket upgrade.
  * `-m {{MAX_CLIENTS}}` — ttyd's default is 0 (UNLIMITED). Always set.
  * NO `-a/--url-arg` — that flag turns the URL into a command-injection vector.

  TMUX ATTACH SEMANTICS
  ---------------------
  * `-L {{TEAM}}` — the team's tmux server runs on a NAMED socket. Omitting -L
    talks to the default server and finds nothing.
  * `attach -t`, never `new -A -s`. `-A` would silently spawn a rogue empty
    session named after an agent, which LCARS would then display as a live
    terminal nobody is driving. Attach must fail loudly when the session is absent.
  * `-f ignore-size` — REQUIRED. Without it an attaching iPad resizes the
    operator's desktop iTerm2 pane to the iPad's dimensions, reflowing an
    agent's terminal out from under it mid-task.

  TMUX_TMPDIR is emitted explicitly because launchd starts jobs with a minimal
  environment. kanban-helpers.sh resolves the socket dir as
  "${TMUX_TMPDIR:-/tmp}/tmux-$(id -u)"; the renderer resolves the same
  expression at render time so the job looks in the same place the team's tmux
  server actually lives.

  ProcessType is deliberately OMITTED (= Standard). `man launchd.plist` states
  Interactive "should only be used if an app's ability to be responsive depends
  on it"; an idle terminal bridge does not qualify, and Background would apply
  I/O throttling we do not want on a keystroke path.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>{{LABEL}}</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>{{TTYD_BIN}}</string>
        <string>-p</string>
        <string>{{TTYD_PORT}}</string>
        <string>-i</string>
        <string>lo0</string>
        <string>-m</string>
        <string>{{MAX_CLIENTS}}</string>
        <string>-H</string>
        <string>X-WEBAUTH-USER</string>
        <string>-b</string>
        <string>{{BASE_PATH}}</string>
        {{WRITABLE_ARG}}
        <string>{{TMUX_BIN}}</string>
        <string>-L</string>
        <string>{{TEAM}}</string>
        <string>attach</string>
        <string>-t</string>
        <string>{{TMUX_SESSION}}</string>
        <string>-f</string>
        <string>ignore-size</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
      KeepAlive: ttyd is a resident server, not a one-shot. Restart it if it
      dies. SuccessfulExit=false means "restart only on abnormal exit" — a clean
      shutdown (e.g. our own uninstall path) is not fought.
    -->
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
        <false/>
    </dict>

    <!--
      ThrottleInterval: damps a crash loop. The realistic failure here is a port
      that is already bound, in which case ttyd exits immediately and launchd
      would otherwise respawn it as fast as it can.
    -->
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>30</integer>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>{{LOG_DIR}}/{{TEAM}}-{{TERMINAL}}.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>{{LOG_DIR}}/{{TEAM}}-{{TERMINAL}}.log</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>{{HOME_DIR}}</string>
        <key>AITEAMFORGE_DIR</key>
        <string>{{AITEAMFORGE_DIR}}</string>
        <key>TMUX_TMPDIR</key>
        <string>{{TMUX_TMPDIR}}</string>
        <!--
          launchd gives a job no locale. Without LANG, tmux/ttyd fall back to a
          non-UTF-8 codeset and box-drawing characters in TUI output arrive as
          mojibake in the pane.
        -->
        <key>LANG</key>
        <string>en_US.UTF-8</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
